<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout xml:id="properties-sets">
  <title>Properties of sets</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      These are properties of sets. You may use these freely in proofs as long as you cite the name of the property.
    </p>
    
    <p>Throughout, let <m>A, B, C</m> be subsets of a universal set <m>U</m>.</p>
  </introduction>

  <ul>
  	<li><p>Properties of the Empty Set and the Universal Set:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>A \cap \emptyset = \emptyset</m></p>
		<p><m>A \cap U = A</m></p>
	</sidebyside>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>A \cup \emptyset = A</m></p>
		<p><m>A \cup U = U</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Idempotent Laws:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>A \cap A = A</m></p>
		<p><m>A \cup A = A</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Commutative Laws:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%"> 
		<p><m>A \cap B = B \cap A</m></p>
		<p><m>A \cup B = B \cup A</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Associative Laws:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>(A \cap B) \cap C = A \cap (B \cap C)</m></p>
		<p><m>(A \cup B) \cup C = A \cup (B \cup C) </m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Distributive Laws:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>A \cap (B \cup C) = (A \cap B) \cup (A \cap C)</m></p>
		<p><m>A \cup (B \cap C) = (A \cup B) \cap (A \cup C)</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Basic Properties:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>(A^{c})^{c} = A</m></p>
		<p><m>A - B = A \cap B^{c}</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Empty Set and Universal Set:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>A - \emptyset = A</m></p>
		<p><m>A - U = \emptyset</m></p>
	</sidebyside>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>\emptyset^{c} = U</m></p>
		<p><m>U^{c} = \emptyset</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>De Morgan's Laws for sets:</p>
	<sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
		<p><m>(A \cap B)^{c} = A^{c} \cup B^{c}</m></p>
		<p><m>(A \cup B)^{c} = A^{c} \cap B^{c}</m></p>
	</sidebyside></li>
	<li><p>Subsets and complements: <m>A \subseteq B</m> if and only if <m>B^{c} \subseteq A^{c}</m></p></li>
	<li><p>Intersection of complements: <m>A \cap A^{c} = \emptyset</m></p></li>
	<li><p>Union of complements: <m>A \cup A^{c} = U</m></p></li>
  </ul>
  
</handout>
